    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4739A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to including Silver\nLake within the definition of \"inland waterways\" for the purposes of\nwaterfront revitalization\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation designates Silver Lake in the County of Wyoming as an\ninland waterway.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends Subdivision 4 of Section 911 of the Executive Law by\nadding Silver Lake to the list of water bodies defined as inland\nwaterways.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nBy defining Silver Lake in the County of Wyoming as an inland\nwaterway, the municipalities and organizations along its banks will be\neligible for Department of State and Environmental Protection Fund\nwaterfront revitalization grants. The opportunity to apply for and\npossibly receive grant monies is of considerable importance to the\nrevitalization efforts of the Silver Lake region.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
